keywords:
  - multi-agent debate
  - scalable oversight
  - LLM-as-a-judge
  - model routing
  - mixture of agents
  - peer critique
  - AI evaluation
abstract: >-
  A working draft proposing what should happen after a panel of AI models is
  convened: the answer has to earn its release. Class-matched tiers of models
  from every major lab decompose a request, bid on its parts, critique each
  other's drafts under seat anonymity with evidence required, and revise until
  they agree. A hub that never writes an answer interrogates the result within
  a question budget and enforces verifiable checks. Release requires agreement,
  no open questions, and passing checks. A persistent, version-stamped
  catalogue records who was challenged, corrected, and later shown wrong. The
  paper positions the design against debate, multi-agent debate,
  mixture-of-agents, LLM-as-a-judge, and routing, and specifies a
  compute-matched pilot that could falsify it.
